    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0167" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3839</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-22T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 24, 7.32 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4042. Department’s 2304, July 17. I am assured, informally, that Swiss Government
                    will accept offer to preside over conference and furnish rooms provided German
                    Government agrees. Does Department deem it advisable to inform German Government
                    that Swiss have been asked to preside?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
